# Data Model & Entity Relationships — {{.ProjectName}}

> **ALWAYS BE DETERMINISTIC. Human approval resolves every decision.**

## 1. Entity-Relationship Diagram

```mermaid
erDiagram
    PROJECT ||--o{ TASK : contains
    TASK ||--o{ EVENT : records
    TASK ||--|| STATE : maintains
    TASK ||--o{ ARTIFACT : produces

    PROJECT {
        string name PK
        string root_path
        string version
    }

    TASK {
        string id PK
        string title
        string typology
        string status
        date created_at
    }

    STATE {
        string task_id PK, FK
        string branch
        string worktree_path
        int input_tokens
        int cache_tokens
        int output_tokens
    }

    EVENT {
        string event_id PK
        string task_id FK
        string event_type
        timestamp timestamp
        string payload
    }

    ARTIFACT {
        string path PK
        string task_id FK
        string artifact_type
        string hash
    }
```

## 2. Entity Dictionary & Lifecycle

### Task
- **Identity:** Unique identifier formatted `T-xxx`.
- **Status Transitions:** `Not started` → `Specifying` → `Awaiting plan approval` → `Implementing` → `Awaiting review` → `Done`.
- **Invariants:** Every task belongs to exactly one typology (`features`, `bugfixes`, `hotfixes`, `spikes`).

### State Snapshot
- **Persistence:** Saved in `.sdd/state/<TASK_ID>/state.json`.
- **Concurrency:** Single-writer atomic file replacement.
